  "type": "numerical",
  "level": 3,
  "question": {
    "text": "A faulty thermometer reads <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>5</mn><mo>&#176;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi></math>&nbsp;in melting ice and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>95</mn><mo>&#176;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi></math>&nbsp;in steam. The correct temperature on absolute scale will be ______ <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">K</mi></math> when the faulty thermometer reads&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>41</mn><mo>&#176;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi></math>.",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [],
  "correctValue": "313",
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>As per&nbsp;working of thermometers,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo>-</mo><mi>L</mi><mi>F</mi><mi>P</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>U</mi><mi>F</mi><mi>P</mi><mo>-</mo><mi>L</mi><mi>F</mi><mi>P</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mtext>constant</mtext></math>.</p><p>Therefore, we can write</p><p>&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mrow><mn>41</mn><mo>&#176;</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>5</mn><mo>&#176;</mo></mrow><mrow><mn>95</mn><mo>&#176;</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>5</mn><mo>&#176;</mo></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>&#176;</mo></mrow><mrow><mn>100</mn><mo>&#176;</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>&#176;</mo></mrow></mfrac></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi>C</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>36</mn><mn>90</mn></mfrac><mo>&#215;</mo><mn>100</mn><mspace linebreak=\"newline\"/><mo>=</mo><mn>40</mn><mo>&#176;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi><mspace linebreak=\"newline\"/><mo>=</mo><mn>40</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>273</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">K</mi><mspace linebreak=\"newline\"/><mo>=</mo><mn>313</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">K</mi></math></p>",
    "image": null
  },
